<ProseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Selected by Men is an editorial desk. Rankings follow a published filter. Product links go to Amazon."
  eyebrow="The desk"
  heading="The ranking is the desk’s. The filter is public."
>
  <p>
    The internet is full of “best of” lists that read like they were written by a
    spreadsheet. Selected by Men exists for a different reader: a man who wants
    a short, honest answer — and who would rather own one excellent thing than
    five forgettable ones.
  </p>
  <p>
    The ranking in every guide is the Selected by Men desk’s ranking. There is
    no masthead of twelve testers and no bathroom diary. The named source of
    that judgment is the filter on <a href="/standards/">Standards</a>: design, a year of use, price against
    materials, verified owner reviews, and whether it is worth telling a friend.
    If a guide is wrong, the guide changes.
  </p>
  <p>
    We cover grooming, style, tech, fitness, home, and everyday carry. The tone
    is practical. The bar is high. If a product does not survive daily use, it
    does not survive the edit.
  </p>

  <h2>How we choose</h2>
  <p>Every recommendation has to clear the same filter:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Is the design considered, or just loud?</li>
    <li>Will it still feel right in a year?</li>
    <li>Is the price honest for the materials and construction?</li>
    <li>Do verified owners report the same strengths we care about?</li>
    <li>Would we tell a friend to buy it?</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The long version — what we look at, what we do not claim, how often a list
    is revisited, and what happens when a pick disappears — lives on <a href="/standards/">Standards</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>About the links</h2>
  <p>
    Product links go to Amazon. That is the storefront, not a side detail. This
    site is an Amazon Associate. Brands cannot buy a ranking. Amazon’s
    commission rate cannot either. The dry version is <a href="/how-we-make-money/">How we make money</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prices, stock, and shipping times change. Always check the retailer page
    before you buy.
  </p>

  <h2>Who this is for</h2>
  <p>
    Men who already have taste, or who want to build it without turning shopping
    into a hobby. You do not need another 40-tab research session. You need a
    point of view.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
